# Staged-file gate. CI (docker-publish.yml `verify`) stays the authority; this
# exists so a broken commit fails where it is written rather than at PR time.
#
# Scope, and why: eslint runs on STAGED FILES only (lint-staged), and typecheck
# runs on the project (tsc has no per-file mode). The full test suite is
# deliberately NOT here — it stands up one PGlite per test file and takes ~90s,
# which nobody waits for on every commit. Run `npm test` before pushing; CI
# holds the line regardless of what this hook lets through.
#
# NO `prettier --write` HERE, deliberately. .prettierrc loads
# prettier-plugin-tailwindcss with tailwindFunctions ["cn","cva"], so formatting
# REORDERS Tailwind class lists — and 12 tests assert literal class strings
# ("uppercase tracking-[0.06em]", "rounded-[3px] bg-primary/10"). An automatic
# format-on-commit rewrites the exact strings those tests match on, turning a
# green suite red with no visible cause. Format on purpose, with the tests in
# view: npm run format.
#
# Bypass for a deliberate WIP commit only: git commit --no-verify
npx lint-staged
npm run typecheck
